## 9. savedStateHandle for cross-fragment data in NavController

```kotlin
// Setting a result from a destination fragment
findNavController().previousBackStackEntry
    ?.savedStateHandle
    ?.set("selected_fund_id", itemId)
findNavController().popBackStack()

// Reading the result in the originating fragment
findNavController().currentBackStackEntry
    ?.savedStateHandle
    ?.getLiveData<String>("selected_fund_id")
    ?.observe(viewLifecycleOwner) { itemId ->
        viewModel.loadFundDetail(itemId)
    }
```

# Input Format

```
App type: multi-activity with XML nav graphs
Activities: [list of activities and their purpose]
Nav graphs: [which graph belongs to which activity]
Deep links: [URL patterns and query params]
Bottom navigation: [tabs and their fragment destinations]
Cross-activity flows: [which flows span activities]
```

# Output Format

```
1. res/navigation/[scope]_nav_graph.xml — per-activity nav graph
2. Activity classes with NavHostFragment setup
3. AndroidManifest.xml — activity declarations + deep link intent filters
4. Safe Args usage for fragment-to-fragment navigation
5. Intent-based cross-activity navigation
```

# Constraints

- This is a MULTI-ACTIVITY app. Do NOT generate single-activity architecture.
- Navigation between activities uses explicit Intents with extras. Do NOT use NavController for cross-activity navigation.
- Navigation within an activity uses Navigation Component with XML nav graphs and Safe Args.
- Deep links always land on SplashActivity. SplashActivity decides whether to route to AuthActivity or MainActivity based on login state.
- Deep link data (DEEPLINK_ID param, FCM extras) is forwarded to MainActivity via Intent extras, then to fragments via NavController bundle.
- Safe Args plugin is used for type-safe fragment arguments. Always use `FragmentDirections` and `FragmentArgs`.
- BottomNavigationView is set up via `setupWithNavController()` in MainActivity.
- All nav graphs are XML-based. Do NOT generate Compose Navigation or type-safe route objects.
- `autoVerify="true"` is set on deep link intent filters for App Links verification.

# Examples

## Input
```
App type: multi-activity with XML nav graphs
Activities: SplashActivity (launcher), AuthActivity (login/register), MainActivity (main content)
Nav graphs: splash_nav_graph, auth_nav_graph, main_nav_graph
Deep links: https://www.example.com/app/?DEEPLINK_ID=123
Bottom navigation: Home, Search, AccountSummary, Profile
Cross-activity flows: Splash→Auth or Splash→Main, Main→Compliance, Main→WebView
```

## Output

```xml
<!-- res/navigation/main_nav_graph.xml -->
<navigation xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    android:id="@+id/main_nav_graph"
    app:startDestination="@id/homeFragment">

    <fragment android:id="@+id/homeFragment"
        android:name=".presentation.ui.fragments.home.HomeFragment"
        android:label="Home">
        <action android:id="@+id/action_home_to_detail"
            app:destination="@id/fundDetailFragment" />
    </fragment>

    <fragment android:id="@+id/searchFragment"
        android:name=".presentation.ui.fragments.fundsearch.FundSearchFragment"
        android:label="Search" />

    <fragment android:id="@+id/portfolioFragment"
        android:name=".presentation.ui.fragments.accountSummary.PortfolioFragment"
        android:label="AccountSummary" />

    <fragment android:id="@+id/profileFragment"
        android:name=".presentation.ui.fragments.profile.ProfileFragment"
        android:label="Profile" />

    <fragment android:id="@+id/fundDetailFragment"
